{
  "id": "loan_processing",
  "title": "Digital personal-loan origination",
  "case_type": "loan processing",
  "scenario": "Head of Retail Lending: We are building a digital personal-loan journey for salaried customers. Applicants fill in an online form, upload their PAN card, address proof and last three salary slips, and should get a decision quickly. Loans up to five lakh rupees are decided automatically by our scoring model; larger loans go to a credit officer for manual review. Credit risk team: The score must use income, existing obligations and bureau history, and we need to be able to explain every decision. Interest rates depend on the applicant's score band. Compliance officer: Declined applicants must receive the specific reason for the decline, and every applicant must see the full interest rate, fees and repayment schedule before accepting the offer. We must verify identity and address and keep the verification records. The scoring model must be reviewed every year for unfair impact on any group of applicants. Customer experience lead: Every application, including the ones that go to a credit officer, must get a final decision within two minutes, so that customers are never left waiting. The form should be simple. Operations: Approved loans are disbursed to the customer's bank account through our existing core banking system. Credit officers need a work queue showing pending applications with the uploaded documents attached. IT security: Uploaded documents contain sensitive personal data and must be encrypted and visible only to credit staff. All decisions and manual overrides must be logged. Product owner: We may add more loan products in future, but the first release covers personal loans only.",
